0	section	Delivering the talisman
0	section	Talking to Archmage Sedridor
1	line	Archmage Sedridor	Welcome adventurer, to the world renowned Wizards' Tower, home to the Order of Wizards. We are the oldest and most prestigious group of wizards around. Now, how may I help you?
1	line	Player	Are you Sedridor?
1	line	Archmage Sedridor	Sedridor? What is it you want with him?
1	line	Player	The Duke of Lumbridge sent me to find him. I have this talisman he found. He said Sedridor would be interested in it.
1	line	Archmage Sedridor	Did he now? Well hand it over then, and we'll see what all the hubbub is about.
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Okay, here you are.
2	line	Player	Okay, here you are.
2	cond	If the player has the talisman:
3	box	You hand the talisman to Sedridor.
3	line	Archmage Sedridor	Hmm... Doesn't seem to be anything too special. Just a normal air talisman by the looks of things. Still, looks can be deceiving. Let me take a closer look...
3	box	Sedridor murmurs some sort of incantation and the talisman glows slightly.
3	line	Archmage Sedridor	How interesting... It would appear I spoke too soon. There's more to this talisman than meets the eye. In fact, it may well be the last piece of the puzzle.
3	line	Player	Puzzle?
3	line	Archmage Sedridor	Indeed! The lost legacy of the first tower. This talisman may in fact be key to finding the forgotten essence mine!
3	line	Player	First tower? Forgotten essence mine? What are you on about?
3	line	Archmage Sedridor	Ah, my apologies, adventurer. Allow me to fill you in.
3	select	Select an option
3	option	Go ahead.
4	line	Player	Go ahead.
4	line	Archmage Sedridor	As you are likely aware, when we cast spells, we do so using the power of runes.
4	line	Archmage Sedridor	These runes are crafted from a highly unique material, and then imbued with magical power from various runic altars. Different altars create different runes with different magical effects.
4	line	Archmage Sedridor	The process of imbuing runes is called runecrafting. Legend has it that this was once a common art, but the secrets of how to do it were lost until just under two hundred years ago.
4	line	Archmage Sedridor	The rediscovery of runecrafting had such a large impact on the world, that it marked the dawn of the Fifth Age. It also resulted in the birth of our order, and the construction of the first Wizards' Tower.
4	line	Player	If it was the first tower, I'm guessing it doesn't exist anymore? What happened?
4	line	Archmage Sedridor	It was burnt down by traitorous members of our own order. They followed the evil god of chaos, Zamorak, and they wished to claim our magical discoveries in his name.
4	line	Archmage Sedridor	When the tower burnt down, much was lost, including an important incantation. A spell that could be used to teleport to a hidden essence mine.
4	line	Player	The essence mine you mentioned earlier, I assume?
4	line	Archmage Sedridor	Precisely. Rune essence is the material used to make runes, but it is incredibly rare. That essence mine was the only place it could be found that our order knew of.
4	line	Archmage Sedridor	Since the incantation was lost, we have struggled to maintain our stocks of rune essence.
4	line	Archmage Sedridor	There are seemingly those out there that still know where to find some, but while they have been willing to sell essence to us, they have refused to share knowledge on how to find it ourselves.
4	line	Player	I'm starting to see why this is so important. So you think this talisman can help you rediscover that incantation?
4	line	Archmage Sedridor	I do! All magic leaves traces, and from what I can tell, this talisman was used heavily during the time of the first tower.
4	line	Archmage Sedridor	It would have been taken to the essence mine many times, and the magical energies there will have left an imprint on it. To think that it was hidden in Lumbridge all this time!
4	line	Player	So what happens now?
4	line	Archmage Sedridor	It is critical I share this discovery with my associate, Aubury, as soon as possible. He's not much of a wizard, but he's an expert on runecrafting, and his insight will be essential.
4	line	Archmage Sedridor	Would you be willing to visit him for me? I would go myself, but I wish to study this talisman some more.
4	select	Select an option
4	option	Yes, certainly.
5	line	Player	Yes, certainly.
5	line	Archmage Sedridor	He runs a rune shop in the south east of Varrock. Please, take this package of research notes to him. If all goes well, the secrets of the essence mine may soon be ours once more!
5	box	Sedridor hands you a package.
5	line	Archmage Sedridor	Best of luck, {player}.
5	cond	If the player gave the talisman to him while doubting his identity:
6	action	end
5	cond	If the player gave the talisman to him without doubting his identity:
6	line	Player	I don't remember telling you my name... How do you know it?
6	line	Archmage Sedridor	Really now? I am the Archmage you know.
6	action	end
4	option	No, I'm busy.
5	line	Player	No, I'm busy.
5	line	Archmage Sedridor	As you wish adventurer. I will continue to study this talisman you have brought me. Return here if you find yourself with some spare time to help me.
5	action	end
3	option	Actually, I'm not interested.
4	line	Player	Actually, I'm not interested.
4	line	Archmage Sedridor	Oh... Well I guess the short of it is that this talisman could be key to helping us rediscover an important teleportation incantation.
4	line	Archmage Sedridor	With it, we'll be able to access a hidden essence mine, our lost source of rune essence.
4	line	Archmage Sedridor	It is critical I share this discovery with my associate, Aubury, as soon as possible. He's not much of a wizard, but he's an expert on runecrafting, and his insight will be essential.
4	line	Archmage Sedridor	Would you be willing to visit him for me? I would go myself, but I wish to study this talisman some more.
4	option	Yes, certainly.
5	action	above
4	option	No, I'm busy.
5	action	above
